      {
        "question": "What should I name my consulting business?",
        "answer": "Most consultants choose one of three shapes: their own name (\"Sarah Rose Consulting\"), which sells you as the expert; a surname-style firm name (\"Hartley & Rowe\"), which sounds established; or a single strong word (\"Keel\", \"Groundwork\"), which leaves room to grow. Add your field (\"HR Consulting\", \"Tax Advisory\") so people know what you do at a glance."
